# API (`apps/api`)

Bun-native server. Do not add Node, `@hono/node-server`, Express, or CORS.

```ts
// ✅ src/index.ts
app.route("/", healthRoutes);
```

- One Hono app per route file (`new Hono()`), then `app.route("/", …)`.
  `src/index.ts` exports `app` for tests and the Bun `default`.
- `requireSession` in `src/middleware/session.ts` is applied per route, not
  with `app.use("*")`. It sets `userId` or returns 401 `{ error }`.
  Membership is next: a missing row or a non-member is 404, never 403.
  `workspace_id` comes from the database row, not from the client.
- Validate params and JSON bodies with `@hono/zod-validator` after
  `requireSession`. Parse responses with `@agentic-kanban/schemas` before
  `c.json`. Invalid input is the validator's 400.
- `src/routes/board.ts` exports `boardRoutes`: board read, task create,
  update, delete, and `POST /api/tasks/:taskId/move`, with the same 401/404
  chain. A `columnId` from another project is 404. Each successful write
  publishes its `BoardEvent` in the route, after the `ForMember` query
  returns and before responding, never inside the transaction: parse the
  task once with `taskSchema` and use that object for the event and the
  response. `projectId` comes from the row and `actorUserId` from the
  session; a 4xx publishes nothing.
- `src/routes/comments.ts` exports `commentRoutes`: `GET` (200) and `POST`
  (201) on `/api/tasks/:taskId/comments`, with `requireSession`, the
  validators, then `listCommentsForMember` / `createCommentForMember`;
  `undefined` is 404. Serialize dates with `toISOString()` and pass the
  response through `commentListResponseSchema` / `commentSchema`. The author
  is `c.get("userId")`, never the body. No WebSocket publish for comments.
  `POST` passes `extractMentionTokens(body)` and `composeMentionEmail`
  (`src/mail/mention.ts`, link from `BETTER_AUTH_URL`) to
  `createCommentForMember`; after the transaction commits it calls
  `deliverEmail` once per notification and `markNotificationEmailed` only
  when that returns `true`. Delivery or marking failures are logged and the
  response is still 201 with the same body.
- `src/mail/index.ts` `deliverEmail({ notificationId, to, subject, text })`
  is the only sending entry point; it never throws and returns whether it
  delivered. With `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, `CLOUDFLARE_EMAIL_TOKEN` and `MAIL_FROM`
  it uses `src/mail/cloudflare.ts` (REST `email/sending/send`, native
  `fetch`; success = 2xx, `success: true`, recipient not in
  `permanent_bounces`; `MAIL_REDIRECT_TO` replaces the recipient and names
  the original in the body; errors are logged without the token). Otherwise
  `src/mail/outbox.ts` appends one JSON line (`to`, `subject`, `body`,
  `notificationId`, `createdAt`) to `OUTBOX_PATH` or `outbox.jsonl` next to
  the `DATABASE_URL` file. Tests delete the four mail variables in
  `test/setup.ts` and inject a fake `fetch`; no SMTP. After delivery the comment `POST` publishes
  `comment.created` with the parsed response and the session actor.
- `src/routes/notifications.ts` (`notificationRoutes`): session first (401),
  then validators. `GET /api/notifications` validates `?before` with
  `notificationListQuerySchema` (400) and calls
  `listNotificationsForRecipient(userId, before)`; `GET
  /api/notifications/unread-count` → `{ count }`; `POST
  /api/notifications/read-all` → `{ updated }`; `POST
  /api/notifications/:notificationId/read` → the row or 404. Dates leave with
  `toISOString()` and every body passes its shared schema.
- Database access only through `@agentic-kanban/db`. Never import
  `@libsql/client` or `drizzle-orm` from the API, including tests.
- API tests use a temporary libSQL file per test file (`src/test/setup.ts`
  calls `migrateDatabase()` before the cached client opens). `test.env` in
  the root `vite.config.ts` sets `NODE_ENV`, the test auth secret,
  `BETTER_AUTH_URL`, and a high `AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_MAX`. The setup also sets a
  temporary `OUTBOX_PATH` and deletes it in `afterAll`. Never use `data/`.
- `src/auth/index.ts` exports `auth`: `drizzleAdapter` on the lazy `db` proxy
  plus `authSchema` (never `getDb()` at module scope). `GET` and `POST`
  `/api/auth/*` delegate to `auth.handler(c.req.raw)` with no zod-validator.
  The built-in in-memory rate limit applies only to sign-up and sign-in
  (`AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_MAX`; `"**": false` last). Do not import `drizzle-orm` in
  the API (the adapter does).
- `src/realtime/index.ts` is the in-memory hub: `subscribe(projectId,
  listener)` returns the unsubscribe; `publish(event)` validates with
  `boardEventSchema.safeParse`, delivers only to that project and never
  throws (invalid events and failing listeners go to `console.error`).
  Realtime stays in this process: no Socket.IO, Redis, or extra service.
- `src/routes/events.ts` exports `eventRoutes` and `boardSocketEvents`.
  `GET /api/projects/:projectId/events` runs `requireSession` (401), param
  + `getProjectForMember` (404), an `Upgrade: websocket` check (426, our
  own: on a failed `server.upgrade` Hono calls `next()`), then
  `upgradeWebSocket` from `hono/bun`. `onOpen` subscribes and sends
  `JSON.stringify(event)`; `onClose` unsubscribes; no `onMessage`.
  `src/index.ts` exports `websocket` next to `fetch`; Bun handles pings
  and the idle timeout. Root `test.alias` points `hono/bun` at its
  WebSocket module because the barrel reads the `Bun` global in Node.
- Do not auto-run migrations or seed. Dev: `bun run --hot`. Listen
  `0.0.0.0:${API_PORT:-3000}`.
